//? Title: PSPNet pyramid context and auxiliary supervision
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Local pixel features can confuse shapes without scene-level context. PSPNet pools several spatial scales and fuses them with dense encoder features. This report checks exact overlapping bins and full graphs,then visibly fits the compact model with explicit main/auxiliary Adam supervision.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/pspnet.cpp`.

> The method

Adaptive1/2/3/6 bins collect global and regional context. Projected,aligned-corner resized means concatenate with dense ResNet features before class prediction. A separate auxiliary head contributes explicitly to the training objective;test predictions use the main head.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/pspnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/pspnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/pspnet_concept.tikz > build/pspnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/pspnet_concept.svg build/pspnet_concept.dvi > build/pspnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
