> Full PSPNet101 and complete auxiliary-head gradients

The encoder is dense output-stride8 ResNet101. Four adaptive pools at1/2/3/6
bins project to512 channels;corner-aligned resizing and the original2048
features concatenate to4096 channels before the3x3/512 fusion head. A linear
classifier restores input-sized logits. A C4 auxiliary classifier supports
supervised training. BN uses momentum.9/epsilon1e-5;full training dropout
keep probability is.9. No pretrained weights are used.

The full model executes67,949,930 learned/110,976 state scalars and all334
tensor gradients below at33px. The compact model retains every pool/head,
ResNet18/divisor8,pool16/head32/aux16,four classes and no dropout. Native
checks require every compact gradient nonzero and exact96/97-pixel main/aux
alignment;all five concatenated context sources contribute.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  {
    n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
    const auto net = m::PSPNet(
        p, state, n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 33 * 33 * 3)).reshape({1, 33, 33, 3}), {}, true);
    const auto g =
        n::grad(n::mean(n::square(net.logits)) + .4 * n::mean(n::square(net.auxiliary)),
                p.parameters());
    if (p.count() != 67949930 || state.count() != 110976 || g.size() != 334 ||
        p.at("head/W").shape() != n::Shape{3, 3, 4096, 512})
      return 1;
    for (const auto &v : g)
      if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()))
        return 1;
    std::print("Full PSPNet101:{} learned/{} state scalars,all{} finite defined gradients "
               "at33px,four pools and auxiliary head.\n",
               p.count(), state.count(), g.size());
  }
  n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
  m::PSPNetConfig c;
  c.classes = 4;
  c.depth = 18;
  c.width_divisor = 8;
  c.pool_width = 16;
  c.head_width = 32;
  c.aux_width = 16;
  c.keep_probability = 1;
  for (int side : {96, 97}) {
    const auto net = m::PSPNet(p, state, n::zeros({1, side, side, 3}), c);
    if (net.logits.shape() != n::Shape{1, side, side, 4} ||
        net.auxiliary.shape() != net.logits.shape())
      return 1;
    std::print(
        "Compact{}px:{} learned/{} state scalars;main/aux align,adaptive bins1/2/3/6.\n", side,
        p.count(), state.count());
  }
}
```
