selected with validation mean IoU.522807. Test pixel accuracy is.875156
and mean IoU.547042;per-class IoUs are background.945169,circle.361144,
rectangle.415453 and triangle.466404. The actual prediction gallery retains
these class confusions rather than implying that high background accuracy
means strong foreground recognition.

\image(figures/pspnet_predictions_1.png)
\caption(Each row shows an actual test image,its truth mask and restored main-head PSPNet prediction. Same palette/range as the fitting preview;errors remain visible.)
\alttext(Four held-out PSPNet image/truth/main-prediction triples.)

> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

\image(figures/pspnet_confusion_api_0.svg)
\caption(Held-out pixel/voxel confusion counts, evaluation 1. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)

\image(figures/pspnet_confusion_api_0_normalized.svg)
\caption(True-class normalized confusion: each nonempty row sums to 100%; zero-support rows remain zero.)
\alttext(Row-normalized percentages with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)


> Conclusion

Exact bin values and every overlap derivative precede full PSPNet101 checks and compact fitting. Explicit auxiliary supervision,fit-only weights,paired BN restoration and actual held-out masks make the measured result inspectable without a benchmark claim.

> References

- [Zhao et al.(2017), Pyramid Scene Parsing Network](https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.01105).
